# 4. Importance of Regression Testing in Agile

Regression testing is very important in Agile because the software is updated frequently. In every sprint, developers may add new features or change existing code. A new change can accidentally affect a feature that was already working properly.

Regression testing helps make sure that **new changes have not broken old functionality**.

### Example 1 – Instagram

Suppose Instagram releases an update to the **Reels** feature. If regression testing is skipped, the update could accidentally affect photo uploading. Users might then face problems while uploading normal posts.

### Example 2 – Zomato

Suppose Zomato changes its **payment or checkout system**. Without regression testing, the change could accidentally affect the restaurant cart or order placement. A user might select food successfully but be unable to complete the order.

**In short:**
Regression testing is important in Agile because frequent changes mean there is a higher chance of affecting existing features. It helps maintain the overall stability of the application after every sprint.

