# 5. Regression Testing After a Payment Module Update – BookMyShow

Suppose the payment module has received a major update. I would test other connected modules because payment is linked with the booking process.

| Module              | Regression Test                                                                    | Expected Result                                                                              |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Seat Selection**  | Select seats, proceed to payment, and return after a successful booking.           | The selected seats should be correctly reserved and should not become incorrectly available. |
| **Booking History** | Complete a booking and then open the Booking History section.                      | The new booking should appear with the correct movie, theatre, seats and booking status.     |
| **Notifications**   | Complete a successful booking and check for the booking confirmation notification. | The user should receive the correct confirmation with accurate booking details.              |

### Final Conclusion

Even though the change was made to the payment module, other modules can be affected because they are connected to the payment process. Running regression tests on **seat selection, booking history, and notifications** helps make sure the complete booking flow still works properly after the update.
